                        "form": "more confiding"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "2dcd16ec-e664-43b3-838b-54a755fa1978",
                        "entry_id": "0b5e1844-5ba5-3d82-a17c-673cf4286ce3",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most confiding"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "abceb0d6-ddcd-33c5-8468-d607df6796f8",
                        "entry_id": "0b5e1844-5ba5-3d82-a17c-673cf4286ce3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having or showing confidence or trust in another person."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4cad0b1d-625e-4395-87e1-524e841c70ab",
                                "sense_id": "abceb0d6-ddcd-33c5-8468-d607df6796f8",
                                "text": "Effingham was by nature indolent, confiding, and, at times, impetuous and indiscreet; but Marmaduke was uniformly equable, penetrating, and full of activity and enterprise."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "86758f83-9270-4097-b72c-fe3fde412dba",
                                "sense_id": "abceb0d6-ddcd-33c5-8468-d607df6796f8",
                                "text": "Those eyes especially struck Eugene, and when he thought of Liza he always saw those clear, mild, confiding eyes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "007c3c26-7ce0-42ae-abb8-0c9d258cc1f2",
                                "sense_id": "abceb0d6-ddcd-33c5-8468-d607df6796f8",
                                "text": "Not having a confiding relationship with one's husband was, however, associated with elevated risk for symptoms of anxiety."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9e15d20c-ddc2-350a-a79f-eec447537db3",
                        "entry_id": "0b5e1844-5ba5-3d82-a17c-673cf4286ce3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In confidence; as if with trust."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "429ea6d7-fe1b-478b-8b97-faa719093bb0",
                                "sense_id": "9e15d20c-ddc2-350a-a79f-eec447537db3",
                                "text": "Sir, they must surely entertain a higher opinion of the credulity of this house, than -- even their recent experience can justify, if they think that their confiding talent will be carried to this length."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6f0dc3d-f51e-4c3e-ba8b-7cb968c71e36",
                                "sense_id": "9e15d20c-ddc2-350a-a79f-eec447537db3",
                                "text": "It might be sufficient, perhaps, to refer only to that trait of frank, confiding generosity, which could overlook all injuries and embrace even former enemies as friends ; as in the case of Saul above referred to ;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "def8cb84-2a26-4a9d-86f7-eb9027d22ac7",
                                "sense_id": "9e15d20c-ddc2-350a-a79f-eec447537db3",
                                "text": "Juliet raised her eyes with confiding tenderness ; there was no interrogation in their glance, yet Montague wished to speak ; his heart was too full for words."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "03e444e7-f432-4ff6-89c2-846a1e19a092",
                                "sense_id": "9e15d20c-ddc2-350a-a79f-eec447537db3",
                                "text": "He defines tie strength in a fairly intuitive way as the amount of time as well as the emotional intensity and intimacy (in a confiding sense, rather than a sexual one, although I don't think he rules out the latter) devoted to our relationships, as well as the mutual benefits characterizing our dealings with other people."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9fe123b7-470f-3501-803c-2c68920e29c0",
                        "entry_id": "0b5e1844-5ba5-3d82-a17c-673cf4286ce3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of a bird, allowing the close approach of humans."
                        ],
